Z||000005||avengador1||12-11-2001||07:17 PM||||Go with the stock AC plugs. I hear they work the best.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||johnt671||12-11-2001||07:49 PM||||I've tried Splitfire that were ok and Rapidfires that made no difference from the Splitfires.  Just went to the +4's and the idle felt better and it seems to run smoother.  I also have an MSD blaster coil and 6a ignition system with Accel 8mm plug wires that may let it take advantage of the platinum plugs.  84 SE.<p>[This message has been edited by johnt671 (edited 12-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||mech312||12-11-2001||07:52 PM||||go with the regular stock ac plugs they work better than all the others||||reg||1
Z||000008||GTDude||12-11-2001||08:15 PM||||I'm a GM auto tech and work on alot of 2.5's in alot of different cars.  From my experience the normal AC plug works best for longevity and performance.  I put whatever kind the customer wants in their car.  More often than not they eventually come back to have AC's put back in.<P>GTDude<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||4
